; ==============================================================================
;  personal.rc  -  your own settings, kept out of the themes
;
;  Copy this file as "personal.rc" into the folder LiteStep runs from (next to
;  step.rc). It is optional: without it the themes use their defaults. It is not
;  part of the repo and tools\deploy.ps1 never touches it.
;
;  step.rc includes it BEFORE the theme, and the first definition of a setting
;  is the one that counts, so anything set here overrides the theme. That works
;  for plain settings ("Key value"); lines that start with * (menus, hotkeys)
;  add to the theme's instead of replacing them.
; ==============================================================================

; Language of the menus and texts. Default: the Windows display language when
; it is one of these, else English: en es pt fr de it zh ja (zh = Simplified
; Chinese). A regional code such as pt-BR or es-CL uses its base language.
; Changing it needs a recycle of LiteStep.
;Language es

; The label in the middle of the top bar (LiteStep Enhanced). Default: your
; Windows user name followed by "'S DESKTOP".
;MUserText "MY DESKTOP"

; Notifications: keep new ones hidden when the column is full instead of
; dropping the oldest.
;NotifyOverflow Wait

; A different notification sound, or none ("").
;NotifySound "C:\path\to\sound.wav"

; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Not settings, but personal too:
;   games\       shortcuts (.lnk, .url) shown under "JUEGOS" in the menu
;   favorites\   shortcuts shown under "FAVORITOS" (managed from the menu itself)
;  Both live in the folder LiteStep runs from.
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
